(footprint "USB_C_Receptacle_HRO_TYPE-C-31-M-12A"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcb-design")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "USB Type-C 2.0 receptacle, HRO TYPE-C-31-M-12A (LCSC C5337088), 16 contacts on 12 SMT lands + 4 PTH shell legs + 2 NPTH alignment holes. AUTHORED, NOT the KiCad stock part - DO NOT SWAP BACK. Source: HRO drawing TYPE-C-31-M-12A REV A dated 2022.10.26 (sha256 fd8a23ee..., 02_parts/TYPE-C-31-M-12A/), view 'RECOMMEND P.C.B LAYOUT (COMPONENT SIDE)', tolerance +/-0.05. The HOLE pattern is copied verbatim from Connector_USB:USB_C_Receptacle_HRO_TYPE-C-31-M-12, which matches the sheet exactly (alignment holes 5.78 apart, shell slots 8.64 apart and 4.18 front-to-rear, front slot drill 1.7 tall, front slot 0.53 above the alignment line). The SMT PAD ROW is RE-LAID because the stock part does NOT match the sheet: stock has pad length 1.45 (sheet 1.14 = 1.64-0.50), wide-pad centres 4.90/6.50 (sheet 4.80/6.40) and the pad centre 1.445 above the alignment line (sheet 1.07) - a 0.375 mm row offset that lands the contact tails off-centre at the heel. Ruled out as an M-12-vs-M-12A variant difference: HRO's base TYPE-C-31-M-12 sheet (C165948, REV A 2020.12.08) carries a dimension-for-dimension IDENTICAL recommended layout. ALIGNMENT-HOLE DIAMETER IS A DECISION, NOT AN INHERITANCE: the sheet's nominal is 0.60 and the moulded post is 2-phi 0.50 (front view). 0.65 is taken - the TOP of the sheet's OWN +/-0.05 PCB-layout tolerance band - because these posts are LOCATORS: at the 0.55 bottom of that band a phi 0.50 post has 0.025 mm radial clearance and a post that will not enter lifts the part off all twelve pads, which is far worse than the 0.075 vs 0.050 mm of lateral play 0.65 permits (and final location is set by reflow self-alignment on 12 pads plus 4 soldered legs, not by the posts). PAD NAMES ARE ALPHANUMERIC A1..B12 + SH ON PURPOSE - tscircuit drops the part silently otherwise (ledger S-COUNT, 2026-07-21); the four merged VBUS/GND lands carry TWO coincident pads each so both contact names reach the netlist. Orientation is fixed by the mouth/board edge and by the asymmetric shell slots (front 2.1 tall, rear 1.6), not by a pin-1 mark.")
	(tags "usb usb-c 2.0 receptacle 16P HRO TYPE-C-31-M-12A smt th hybrid")
